{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310851,"nonce":"sTEdP9hyGZA0xV5Yfi9lzDWIv9c=","title":"Concurrent spokes are blocked BY THE TYPE SYSTEM: LlamaModel does not derive Send. The compiler emits the exact worklist (spinPool, ...","message":"**ESTABLISHED 2026-08-19** (10-agent map/design/adversarial-verify pass, then every\nload-bearing claim re-checked by hand against the code — two agents contradicted\neach other and the verifier was right).\n\n\n`SpinPool` has ONE set of control cells (`cursor`, `rowsCell`, `chunkCell`,\n`pending`), ONE closure field `_fn`, and one boolean state bit per worker with no\ndispatch identity or generation (SpinPool.hx:82-87). Two concurrent callers give:\n\n- `_fn` is a plain field store (:337) read by the worker only when it sees\n  `state == 1` (:208-210) — **a worker woken by A can run B's closure**, and\n  because `_fn` is written BEFORE rows/chunk (:337 vs :351-352), it can run B's\n  band against A's row count ⇒ **out-of-bounds writes**, not merely wrong numbers.\n- `cursor().store(0)` (:350) rewinds a cursor in-flight workers are claiming from\n  (:175) ⇒ rows computed twice, tail rows never claimed. Breaks the bit-identical\n  guarantee the class doc sells at :20-24.\n- `pending` is an absolute store (:353) decremented by every worker (:214), so the\n  join (:369) is pool-global — **a caller can be released while its own band is\n  still running** and read a half-written tensor, silently.\n- Lost wakeup: the worker's `stateC.store(0)` (:213) erases a flip a second\n  dispatcher just wrote (:357). The reset-before-decrement ordering documented at\n  :28-32 only defends the SEQUENTIAL re-dispatch case.\n- Park permits are a single std token (concurrency.rs:325-329) — two unparks\n  coalesce into one.\n- `lastDispatchUs`/`gapEwmaUs` (:326-336) are pool-wide and non-atomic, so each\n  dispatcher measures the gap to the OTHER's call. That EWMA sizes both the tight-\n  spin floor (:256-258) and the idle hold (:270-271).\n\n\n**1. PROCESS-GLOBAL MUTABLE SCRATCH IN THE KERNEL PATH.** Verified by hand:\n`Q4Matmul.hx:556-557` `static var _w16/_x16`; `FlashDecode.hx:121-124`\n`static var _bq/_bqs/_bsc/_bv`. These are process-wide and are grown/FREED in\nplace, so two spokes race the POINTER, not just the contents — spoke A holding an\naddress while spoke B frees it is a use-after-free. **No pool design fixes this.**\n\n**2. THERE IS A SECOND DISPATCHER, IN RUST.** `rayzor-tensors/src/worker_pool.rs`\nhas its own `parallel_rows` (:222) and a telling `parallel_rows_no_nest` (:505).\nSo \"one pool per spoke\" does NOT isolate — the Rust pool is still shared.\n\n\n- **Leased pool (serialize dispatch):** `matmulFused` recursively calls the public\n  `matmul` (Q4Matmul.hx:2121-2125), so a lease held across a whole matmul\n  self-deadlocks. NOTE: this refutes THAT SKETCH, not serialization itself — a\n  lease scoped to a single `parallelRows` dispatch does not nest (Q4Matmul\n  dispatches sequentially; no `parallelRows` is called from inside a band).\n- **Pool per spoke:** \"zero shared dispatch state\" is false (blocker 2 above).\n  Also statically partitions cores, and `shutdown()` from a non-owning thread is a\n  deadlock + use-after-free on the freed control block (:442-454, join at :369).\n- **Lane-multiplexed:** deleting per-worker drained state leaves `armOf(l)` set for\n  the whole tail, so workers re-enter the steal loop every spin iteration — a\n  P-1-way atomic storm on exactly the cells real claimants need, landing in the\n  very window the design claims to monetise.\n\n\nNo `Thread.spawn` anywhere under `nue/nue`. `newSession`/`forwardIdsWith` have\nexactly ONE caller: `examples/kv-session-smoke/Main.hx`. The server\n(`examples/llama-chat-server`) accepts ONE connection at a time and drives the\nattention modules' own caches. So concurrent spokes are unbuilt work, and the\nstatic-state removal is the bulk of it.\n\n\n1. Remove process-global mutable state from the kernel path (session- or\n   lane-keyed scratch). **Required by every design; do it first.**\n2. Then the cheapest correct pool is a lease scoped to ONE dispatch.\n   [[project_moe_expert_locality_measured]] measured that interleaving spokes per\n   LAYER scores within 0.2 pt of per TOKEN, so serializing dispatch costs nothing\n   in cache terms — the usual objection to it is measured and dead.\n3. Independent cheap candidate (verify before believing): every dispatch unparks\n   EVERY worker (SpinPool.hx:356-359, gated only on `pid != 0`, not on actually\n   being parked), and `rayzor_thread_unpark` takes a process-wide `PARKABLE.lock()`\n   (concurrency.rs:352-358) ⇒ ~850 global mutex acquisitions per token, mostly\n   no-ops. Gating on a real `parked` flag is ~20 lines and orthogonal to all of the\n   above. NOT yet measured — on a 62 ms token this may be well under 1%.\n\n---\n\n\nWriting the concurrent test (`Thread.spawn` decoding two sessions) does not\nproduce corruption — **it does not compile**:\n\n    [E0302] Cannot send value of type `nue.arch.LlamaModel` across threads:\n            type does not derive Send\n\nDeriving `@:derive([Send, Sync])` on LlamaModel as a DIAGNOSTIC makes the\ncompiler print the entire transitive worklist:\n\n- `spinPool` not Send/Sync\n- `metadata` not Send/Sync\n- `embedTokens` not Send/Sync\n- `blocks` (Array\u003cLlamaBlock\u003e) not Send/Sync\n- and separately: `KVSession` not Send\n\n**That list IS the multi-spoke worklist, enforced.** Do not hand-audit for shared\nmutable state — derive Send on the type you want to share and let the checker\nenumerate it. (Revert the derive afterwards; asserting Send that does not hold\nwould manufacture exactly the corruption it claims to prevent.)\n\n\nFull census of mutable statics under `nue/nue` (grep `^\\s*static var ` minus\n`static inline`). Three categories:\n\n- **Env-gate memoization** (`_int8`, `_haxeMatmul`, `_amx`, `_enabled`, ...):\n  write-once, idempotent. Benign.\n- **Telemetry counters** (`_census*`, `_plan*`, `_ds*`, `_sProj`): lossy under\n  concurrency, but not a correctness hazard for results.\n- **SCRATCH BUFFERS — the only real hazard**, and there are SEVEN, not the six an\n  agent pass named:\n  - `Q4Matmul._w16/_x16` (:556-557) — AMX **prefill** only\n  - `Q4Matmul._f16Scratch` (:630) — **DEAD**, `f32ToF16()` has ZERO callers; only\n    the safe `f32ToF16At(v, callerScratch)` is used. Its own doc already says a\n    shared static here would race across pool workers.\n  - `FlashDecode._bq/_bqs/_bsc/_bv` (:121-124) — touched ONLY by `decodeBatch`\n    (batched/**prefill**)\n\n**`FlashDecode.decode` (the single-token DECODE path) uses `kc.scrQ/scrQScale/\nscrScores/scrV` — INSTANCE fields on Q8Cache (Q8Cache.hx:24-27), and\n`KVCache.cloneEmpty` builds fresh Q8Caches. So steady-state decode is ALREADY\nsession-clean.** Only prefill carries process-global scratch, which means a first\nharness can serialize prefill (bursty, once per request) and leave decode alone.\n\n---\n\n\n**Increment 1 DONE.** `SpinPool` now takes a **dispatch lease** — cell 10, with\nthe per-worker base shifted 10 -\u003e 11 (`stateOf`/`pidOf`/`busyUsOf`/`claimsOf`\nand `cells =` in the ctor all move together). Acquire after the degenerate\nearly-returns and before ANY control-cell write; release after the join.\nWaiters `Thread.yieldNow()` rather than spin — a waiting dispatcher does no\nuseful work and would steal a core from the band it is waiting for.\n\nPut in a CELL, not a field, deliberately: adding members to a class in this\nposition has twice caused cross-module id drift ([[bugs_preexisting_ranked_2026_08_10]],\nand `Parker.hx` exists only because of it).\n\nVerified: 184/184 suite, llama-chat tokens byte-identical, kv-session-smoke\nstill PASSES, no `LLVM upgrade failed`. Perf A/B interleaved 4x: base mean 98.6\nvs lease 103.1 tok/s — box too contaminated (1.4 GB free, 8 GB swap) to resolve\na sub-1% effect, but no large regression. The lease is one uncontended CAS +\none store per dispatch.\n\n**Scoped to ONE dispatch, which is what makes it safe:** Q4Matmul dispatches\nsequentially and no `parallelRows` runs inside a band, so it never nests. A\nlease across a whole matmul WOULD deadlock (`matmulFused` -\u003e `matmul`).\n\n\n`scratchBytes(slot,size)` (SpinPool.hx:~396) hands EVERY caller the same three\nbuffers, and Q4Matmul quantizes into one then bands over it — so the buffer is\nheld ACROSS the dispatch (Q4Matmul.hx:1290-1292, 1422/1424, 1592/1594,\n2085/2087, 2147). The per-dispatch lease does NOT cover that window: spoke B can\ntake the lease between spoke A's two dispatches and overwrite A's scratch.\nDecode uses these sites (batch=1), so this blocks concurrent DECODE.\n\nTwo candidate fixes, neither started:\n\n1. **Per-lane scratch.** `Thread.currentId()` exists (Thread.hx:96, mapped to\n   `Thread_currentId`). Lane = CAS on a per-lane owner cell; buffers indexed\n   `lane*3+slot`. RISKS: needs new SpinPool FIELDS (append only — never reorder),\n   and `Array\u003cBytes\u003e` with null entries is a shape this file deliberately avoids\n   (it uses `Null\u003cBytes\u003e` fields + `cast` instead).\n2. **REENTRANT lease** (owner-thread + depth cells) taken at the CALLER around\n   the whole scratch lifetime. Reentrancy is what makes the `matmulFused` -\u003e\n   `matmul` recursion safe, so the lease can be coarser than one dispatch.\n   Serialises a whole matmul instead of one dispatch — and\n   [[project_moe_expert_locality_measured]] measured that interleave granularity\n   does not affect cache locality, so that costs nothing there. RISK: bracketing\n   5+ call sites that have early returns and live `throw`s; a leaked lease is a\n   deadlock. Wants RAII, which Haxe does not give here.\n\n`pooled = sp != null` (Q4Matmul.hx:1289) already selects a correct\nalloc-per-call path, but `sp` is also the dispatcher so it cannot just be nulled.\n\n\n`spinPool` (needs increment 2 first), `metadata`, `embedTokens`,\n`blocks` (Array\u003cLlamaBlock\u003e — note `GQAttention.cache` is a mutable field, so\nSync is a lie until sessions are the ONLY KV owner), and `KVSession` -\u003e Send.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_multispoke_pool_not_the_blocker` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}